{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     page/injection — restore the code injection Ghost skips on an index.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     ⚠ CALL THIS FROM EVERY TEMPLATE NAMED BY A COLLECTION WITH `data: page.x`.

     Ghost runs a page's codeinjection_head / codeinjection_foot for the
     resource it treats as that request's context. On a collection index the
     context is the COLLECTION, not the page bound to it with `data:` — so the
     injection is skipped entirely.

     That is a silent failure of the worst kind: the fields still show the code
     in Ghost Admin, the page renders, nothing errors, and whatever was pasted
     there — analytics, structured data, a search-console verification tag —
     is simply absent from the HTML. The only way to notice is to view source
     and know what should have been there.

     The fix is to render it ourselves into the two slots default.hbs opens.
     Lifted from namaste-salesforce-bright, which documents the same trap.

     ⚠ TRIPLE-STASHED, deliberately. This is author-supplied HTML and must not
     be escaped — {{codeinjection_head}} would render the markup as visible
     text. It is the site owner's own field, written by whoever can already
     edit templates, so the trust boundary is the same one Ghost applies.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
{{#contentFor "head-after"}}
    {{#page}}{{#if codeinjection_head}}{{{codeinjection_head}}}{{/if}}{{/page}}
{{/contentFor}}

{{#contentFor "foot-after"}}
    {{#page}}{{#if codeinjection_foot}}{{{codeinjection_foot}}}{{/if}}{{/page}}
{{/contentFor}}
